  "answer": "The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Changes\n\n**`tags.mjs`** — Implemented `parseTags(input)` (kept the named export):\n\n1. **Type check**: Throws `TypeError` if `input` is not a string.\n2. **Split**: Uses `input.split(',')` — splits only on literal commas.\n3. **Normalize each part**:\n   - `.trim()` removes surrounding JavaScript whitespace.\n   - `.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` collapses each nonempty internal whitespace run to a single ASCII space.\n   - `.toLowerCase()` lowercases via `String.prototype.toLowerCase()`.\n4. **Discard empties**: Skips parts that normalize to `''`.\n5. **Deduplicate**: Uses a `Set` for case-sensitive comparison after normalization, preserving first-occurrence order.\n\n## Verification against public tests\n\n- `'red,blue,green'` → `['red', 'blue', 'green']` ✓\n- `'  Red , , BLUE  ,'` → `['red', 'blue']` (trims, lowercases, drops empties) ✓\n- `'Alpha,beta,alpha,BETA,gamma'` → `['alpha', 'beta', 'gamma']` (dedupes `alpha`/`Alpha` and `beta`/`BETA`) ✓\n- Empty/delimiter-only strings return `[]` ✓\n\nThe public tests were not modified.",
